Title: The House 
Credit: Written By
Author: Justin Del Vecchio
Draft date: May 2026

INT. COFFEE SHOP - MORNING
Brilliant morning.  Coffee shop similar to a Dunkin Donuts.  Mixture of people and kids going to school, etc.  

MIKA BOYKO is in line.  He is in his early 60s, Ukranian accent.  He is annoyed and looks disapprovingly at person in front of hime.  The cutomer oblivously checks phone while cashier holds out change for purchase.

MIKA
Ahem

CUSTOMER
Oh hey, thanks! Thanks!

Collects change and moves along.  Mika places two dollars and one quarter on counter.

MIKA
Hi, ususal.


Mika takes coffee, finds table and sits with two friends.  Older, clearly retirees.

FRIEND 1
Hey Mika, ho are you doing.

MIKA
OK.  Got up early, wathced sun rise, and walked here.  Traffic ridiculous today.  Crazy.  People speeed like made right by school.

FRIEND 2
Hey, how did the house go.

MIKA
I knew you would bring up.  Knew it was, three months, right?

FRIEND 1
(smiling)
Seems longer than that!


Mikas hands cover and rub face.

MIKA
Is not.  Is just three months.  Since that St. Patrick's Day nonsense.  Heh ... and it has not. It has not!

FRIEND 3
What is the house.  What's that? 

FRIEND 2
Oh come on ...

Mika holds up both hands as if to say all is ok

MIKA
I will explain.  The house. What is the house. OK. The house is my wife's parnets.  Wonderful people.  You hear stories about mouther-in-law and trouble.  She would do anything for you - no trouble at all.  

Mika sips coffee

MIKA
She would do anything for us.  Her husband, he died back in the 90s.  Smoked like you would not believe.  The mothe, she died in February.

FRIEND 3 
Sorry about that

MIKA
Yeah, yeah.  Thanks.  So ... we get the house.  Nona has one sister.  She lives in Austinn and she tells Nona 'You sell the house.  Keep the money.  I lived in Austin for last 22 years - you took care of mama.  You should keep it."  The sister, she got some money from the mother and did not, mind you, need to clean out all the shit from house.

FRIEND 2
You got a house my friend!  A house!  House partry.  Easy money.


Friend 3 says in passing 
FRIEND 3
Austin ...

MIKA
Yeah, easy money.  And Austin is OK place.  Visited my sister-in-law there four or five times.  Visted twice in Juyly.  Crazy. Hot, hot, hot.  Cannot leave house in daytime, could only leave at night.  Reminded me of Egypt where people in the summer can only go outside at tnight.  

Mika pauses for more coffee

MIKA
Coffee is weak today.  Who make this!  Ok, so, that is alll good.  All fine.  Sister OK with everything.  Wife OK with everything.  All  we need to do is sell house, get money, move on.

Immediately break

INT.  Kitchen of an older tudor home.  Mika is inside with his wife Nona.  Nona is impeccabily dressed.  She is beautiful.  Both sit at the kitchen table.  For some reason Nona is eatin a sausage McMuffin.

MIKA
All he have to do is sell the house.  Put it on the market.  Set a reasonable price, I know what that price is, and we are good.

NONA
I know.  I know!  we can see the house and then, we can think about a condo in Ft. Lauderdale.

MIKA
I keep telling you - there is no way we can get a anything good in Ft. Lauderdal for the price we can get for this house no way -

NONA
(finishing McMuffin)
You keep saying that.  But you are not looking hard enough. I see these shows.  I see the Beachfront Bargins, they find these things all the time.  I will find something, let me look.

MIKA
You can look all you want.  All you want.  I will not stop you from doing that.  Dowload the app, search Ft. Lauderdale.  There is nothing to had for $200 thousand.  Not even close.  Its just ... its not even realistic!

NONA
Exactly, because you do not let me look.  You are not looking right.

Mika shakes head, exhales, and looks away.

MIKA
Let's just sell this thing first.  Please.  Let's do that.  Then we can argue about Ft. Lauderdale.

NONA
Yes, let's talk about the house.  I know exactly what we need to do.

MIKA
Good, good.  Consensus.  I know too.

NONA
Really, you know what to do.  You have read my mind and know.  Really.

MIKA
Yes, I have.  I have looked at the prices. Houses, comprables.

Nona shaiking head
NONA
Comprables.  

MIKA
Yes.  Yes.  We should put a good price on the house.  Go $240K or $245K to start and get offers.  Move it out.

NONA
Really.  That is what we should do.

MIKA
Yes.  Really.

NONA
(smiling confidently) This is what we are going to do.

MIKA
No ... no.

NONA
We are going to use Mikey Drogai.

MIKA
No, no. Why.  No.  Why?  Why Mikey?

NONA
Beacuse, he is a real estate agent.  He knows how to sell a house.  And he knows how to get the best price. And we know his family.

MIKA
Oh great!  Great.  So you are providing the precise reasons we should not go with Mikey.  What if things go wrong.

NONA
What do you mean, wrong? 

MIKA
Mikey is not bale to the house, he listens to you and prices it waty to high, and he get exactly no one interested and looking that the house.  I know this kid, we know this kid, we know exactly what he is capable of.

NONA
He sold Mideas house.  Two weeks.  Two weeks and the house was sold.  We will have no problems.  None.

MIKA
Oh come on.  Midra's house was perfect.  Perfect.  Updated kitchen, huge yard, you could fit three cars in that garage.  I could have sold that house.  Easy to do.  Your parent's house, this house, not easy.

NONA
(Smiling).  No.  No. This house is perfect.  It is great. There will be no problems. 

MIKA
It is not great.  Not gret.  Not not great.  Its good, its a good house, yes.  But it has problems.

NONA
Like what?

MIKA
Like the fact the kitchen is out of a 1970s Reader's Digest advertisement.  Like the fact there are three bathrooms with pink tiles.  Pink tiles.  Like the fact every square inch of flooring that is not bathroom is carpeting from the 1980s -  

NONA
(Smiling) You can stop now.  I do not need to listen to this.  This house, this house, is perfect.  It will sell.  Besides, I have already called Mikey.

MIKA
How? When? Why did you do this and not ask me?

NONA
Uh, because, I do not need your permission.  Is my house. I make the deicisions.

MIKA
You do not need my permission that is not what I said. 

NONA
Sure sounded like it.

MIKA
Not my permission, just my advice.

NONA
There is some difference between the two?

MIKA
Yes, of course.  Of course there is.  I would have told you 'Mikey, I don't think he is a good choice.'  I see realtors online, I think I know which ones are good.  We get that flyer from the Spencer woman, she seems like she knows how to sell a house.

NONA
Well (laughing) we meet Mikey tomorrow.

MIKA
When?

NONA
4PM at my parent's house.

MIKA 
Opportunity to discuss?

NONA
Nope.  Do you want more coffee.

MIKA
Please ... yes.


EXT. Mika is outside a plain looking house built in the early 1970s.  He looks at his watch which reads 4:20.  A large 4 door back BMW with tinted windows wheels in.  Vantiy plat with Drogai2 pulls in.  Mikey steps out.  He is tall, close to 6'2.  He is nice looking and wears gray slacks with tan trench coat.  He sets cup of coffee on top of car as he takes off sunglasses.  He then confidently walks to Mika, carrying an attache case.

MIKEY
(booming voice)  Mika!  Nona!  It is so good to seeyou!  

Mikey moves in for a hug and a giddy Nona goes over for an embrace.

NONA
Oh Mikey, so glad you can help!  So great.  How are you!  How is everything!  

MIKEY
Oh Non, it could not be better.  Could not be better!  Look!

Mikey gestures to BMW and then goes to shake hands with MIKA

MIKA
You are late.  20 minutes.  Late.

MIKEY
Ohhhh, so sorry.  So sorry.  I had to take the kids to hockey practice.  It went late.  I wanted to call but I only had your home number and figured you would already be here. 

MIKA
And yet you have coffee.

MIKEY
(Walking with Nona) Yeah, they sell it at the rink.  What did we do here!

NONA
Don't worry about being late.  We have nothing to do.  Look, I cleand up the orn of the house.

MIKEY
Oh every littel bit helps Nona.  Every little bit.  This, this, this is a great house.  Great house!

MIKA
Yes, good house.  Not great though.  But good.

MIKEY
No, no, do not undersell this house. This (looking at the house) is a great house.

Mikey makes a gesture with his hand as though taking a picture.

NONA.
See!  I keep telling him it is great Mikey but he will not listen. He will not listen.

MIKEY
Don't worry Nona, we'll win him over

(both start laughing)

MIKEY
I already know the price for the house.

MIKA
What?  How they hell do you know the price for this house.  You haven't step foot in here, in, what 17 years?  Again, how the hell do you know?

MIKEY
Mika.  Mika!  I know real estate!  I know this stuff.  I looked at the pictures on Google Maps.  I know the exact price.  Nona
(looking to Nona) I know the exact price for this beautiful house, I know.

NONA
Oh Mikey, I know you do.  I know you do.  Come on, let's look at.

MIKA
Why bother? He know price.  He doesn't need to look at anything.  By the way, uh, what exactly is the price.  The pefect price.

Mikey stands.  Hands at hip.  Taking snapshot pose with hand he looks to Nona. 

MIKEY
The price.  The price is 320.  320 and not a nickle less.

NONA
Yes!

MIKA
Oh come on! 

MIKEY
Absolutely.  No doubt!  The price is 320 and we can close this baby, smooth deal, in two weeks.

MIKA
You haven't even looked insided.  Mikey, I am sorry.  But you are crazy if you think you are gonna get 320 for thsi house its - it 

MIKEY
Nona.  Listen to this guy.  Listen to him!

(slaps Mika on the back a bit too hard)

MIKEY
The house will sell.  For 320.  I know real estate.  I live and breathe this stuff.  This house will sell for 320.  No doubt.

NONA
I knew it.  That will set us up for something special in Ft. Lauderdale.

MIKA
Its not going to sell for that.  Never going to sell.  And even if it did, we get nothing special in Ft. Lauderdale for that amount.  Sorry.  Nothing.

(looking to Mikey)

Please, set the price lower.  

MIKEY
Why go low when you can go high and get the price you want.  The price you need!

MIKA
Mikey, house is not worth that amount.  It should be 240 to 245 at most.  At most.  Make your life.  God, make our life easy.  Just start at a reasonable price, sell it fast and get it done.

MIKEY
Why 240 may I ask.  Why that price?

MIKA
First, the interior is outdated.  All the rooms, all the rooms need rennovations.  All every last one.  Have seen the popcorn ceilings in there.

MIKEY
Ahhhh.... but the house has a good layout.  It has a great layout.  You can't beat that.  And some people like that 70s stuff it is coming back.

MIKA
You haven't been in this friggin house in 17 years.  Why don't you walk through.  Just imagine you have this mental calculator that figures out renos costs. 10, 20, 30, very quickly you get to 60, 60 thousand in renos to make families who live in this neighborhood happy.

MIKEY
Exactly, its a great neighborhood.

MIKA
Yeah, it is, it is.  Have you looked at the comprables.  Have you seen houses with this square footage?  Look at how good they are on the interior.  This is, a joke,

Mikey laughs

MIKEY
Comprables.  Nona, you did not tell me that Mika had a side hustle as a real estate agent.  You should have told me!

NONA
Oh Mikey, lets go inside and look.  The coffee maker is still that.  I made coffee and have dansih for you.

MIKA
I am not a fan of danish.

NONA
Mikey is.

Mika turning attention back to Mikey

MIKA
Mikey, I go two blocks that way and find houses with the same amount of space, less traffic, no updates needed, they go for 2-9-9.  Why the hell would this go for 340.

MIKEY
You forget about the intangibles.

MIKA
What?  What?  What intangibles?  What, that is on high traffic street with crappy interier.  It on Main Street.  Mikey, Main Street.  Every town has a Main strett it is one thing; busy.

MIKEY
Excatly, benefit one.  Its on Main Street.

MIKA
So?

MIKEY
Zoned residential 

(turns to look at Nona and points to house)

MIKEY
And commerical.

MIKA
So!

MIKEY
You just doubled your market my frient.  Doubled it.  It could work for a familty or professional or doctor or lawyer - 

MIKA 
Yes, because lawyers are so interested in doing home renovations and not in sending you $300 invoice for a half hour of work to send you a letter that the will reading date has been set.  Yeah, they love renovations.

NONA
Mika, please listen to Mikey.

MIKA
What?

MIKEY
Mika, Mika, lets look inside the house.  I am going to show how we are going to get 3-2-0 for this. 

(Group headsup driveway.  Mikey opens door to house out of 1971.

MIKEY
This house.  This house!  What a layout, just as I remembered it.  People are going to love it.

MIKA
Or, or.  They might just walk through this door and this 'This is a lot of work.'

Mikey disregards comment.  Sets coffee down and produces a camera. As he chats with Nona he then takes one pic.  He next heads to the kitchen and takes one pic, still chatting with Nona.)

Mika proceeds to walk through the mostly empty house and peeks into outdated bathrooms and heavily wood paneled rumpus room with a massive, outdate stero player.

MIKEY
And whose bedroom was this?

NONA
Stellas.  Stella.  She had this wall covered with posters of bands, it was quite beautiful how she laid it out.  She was always an artist.  Thats why she is Austin now.

MIKEY
Oh Austin, thats a place we might want to move to!  The market there is so hot.

Mikey againk takes on pic of the room and moves on.

MIKA
One picture.

MIKEY
Hmmm?

MIKA
One pic.  Each room you take one pic.  Why not take more than that?  You know, a selection to choose from.

MIKEY
Again,  I am a real estate agent.  I know this stuff.  One and done!

NONA
They are all signed.  All papers are signed.  You are our agent Mikey!

Mika, resigned, sitting at the kitchen table.

MIKA
Ok

MIKEY
Hey, where is the pool table?  Is it still here?  In the basement.

NONA
Yes, its still there!  We couldn't sell it during the estate sale.  It goes with the house.

MIKEY
Oh, bonus.  Hey, I'm going to play a game.

Mikey heads to the basement with Nona.  

MIKA
Why not take more pictures.


